# Illustrator JSX Rules

## Script Safety
- NEVER modify the source `.ai` file destructively
- NEVER delete layers or objects from the source
- Always export TO a designated output folder (not the source folder)
- Show an alert/dialog if the script completes successfully or fails

## Layer Naming Convention
- Room layers: `room_{name}` (e.g., `room_kho`, `room_sanh_chinh`)
- Props layers: `props_{room_name}`
- Reference layers: `ref_{description}`
- Guide layers: `guide_{description}`

## Export Settings
- SVG 1.1 profile
- Preserve layer names as group IDs
- Embed no raster images
- Flatten transforms where possible
- Output to `assets/2d/svg_raw/` by default

## Compatibility
- Target Illustrator CC 2020+ (ExtendScript)
- Use `$.writeln()` for debug logging (appears in ESTK console)
- Use `alert()` for user-facing messages
- Test with both CS6 and CC if possible

## File Organization
- One script per purpose (export, organize, batch, transform)
- Include header comment with: name, purpose, author, date, version
- Include `#target illustrator` directive
